# Always use Context7 & Ponytail Guidelines

## Context7
Whenever using libraries, frameworks, SDKs, or APIs (e.g. React, Next.js, Express, TailwindCSS, etc.):
- Always refer to Context7 to look up current, version-accurate documentation and code examples.
- Use `ctx7 library <name> "<topic>"` to find the library ID and `ctx7 docs <library-id> "<query>"` to fetch docs.
- Ground all code in Context7 documentation.

## Ponytail (Lazy Senior Developer Mode)
The best code is the code never written. Follow the ladder:
1. YAGNI (does this need to exist?)
2. Reuse existing code in this codebase.
3. Standard library first.
4. Native platform feature over libraries.
5. Already-installed dependency.
6. One line if possible.
7. Only then: minimum working code.
- No unrequested abstractions or boilerplate. Deletion over addition.
- Shortest working diff wins.
- Fix root cause, not symptom.
- Never compromise security, data safety, or accessibility.
